      "id": "7cfde4ccf71b",
      "name": "Morning Briefing \u2014 Email + Daily Note",
      "prompt": "Create the daily Morning Briefing for the Clawbot Obsidian vault at `/Users/absorbo/Library/Mobile Documents/iCloud~md~obsidian/Documents/Obsidian`.\n\nImportant paths:\n- Daily note: `01 - Daily Notes/YYYY-MM-DD.md` for today's local date.\n- Daily note template: `90 - Templates/Daily Note.md`.\n- Gmail script: `/Users/absorbo/.hermes/skills/productivity/google-workspace/scripts/google_api.py`.\n- M365 script: `/Users/absorbo/.hermes/skills/productivity/m365-graph/scripts/m365_graph_mail.py`.\n- Python: `/Users/absorbo/.hermes/hermes-agent/venv/bin/python3`.\n\nTasks:\n1. Create today's daily note from the template if it does not exist. Substitute template placeholders with actual values; do not write literal `{{...}}` placeholders.\n2. Fetch unread Gmail with query `is:unread`, max 30.\n3. Fetch unread M365 mail by listing recent inbox messages and filtering `isRead == false`, max 30. If M365 search is unavailable, use list + Python filtering.\n4. Email resilience: if Gmail fails, continue with M365. If M365 fails, continue with Gmail. If both fail, write that email is unavailable.\n5. Triage emails into: \ud83d\udd3a Action Required, \u23eb Important, \ud83d\udd3c FYI, \ud83d\udd3d Ignored.\n6. For \ud83d\udd3a and \u23eb emails, read full message/thread where safe and cross-reference vault for customer/project context.\n7. Write briefing only inside the `## \ud83d\udcec Morning Briefing` section of today's daily note.\n8. Draft reply text in the note when useful, but do not send any email.\n\nHard constraints:\n- \u26d4 NEVER delete email. EVER. No exceptions. Not trash, not deleted items.\n- \u26d4 NEVER send email. Draft text only.\n- \u26d4 NEVER modify email labels, read state, folders, or metadata.\n- \u26d4 NEVER assume context; use `[CONFIRM: ...]` placeholders for uncertainty.\n- \u26d4 NEVER modify content outside `## \ud83d\udcec Morning Briefing`.\n- \u26d4 NEVER modify templates or archives.\n\nFinal output: short status summary with